# p_d9a2 — The 18:30 cook: pan leaves the cupboard late, mug hits the coffee table early (fork of p_789a)

Forked from p_789a to fix two timing errors. The parent places the pan on the counter from 17:30, but the 18:00 patrol finds it still in cupboard_k1 and the 19:00 patrol finds it on counter_k1. The cooking window is therefore 18:00–19:00, with the pan hitting the counter partway through (≈18:15–18:30). Similarly, mug_omar is already at coffee_table_l1 at 18:00, meaning the evening transition to the living room begins before the 19:30 TV block the parent assumes.

What changed from the parent:
- Pan: cupboard 0–18.5, counter 18.5–19.5 (was counter 17.5–19).
- Pot: cupboard 0–18.5, counter 18.5–19.5 (was counter 17.5–19).
- Mug_omar: coffee_table_l1 from 18:00 (was 19:00).
- Snack bowl: counter_k1 at 18:00 (dinner prep), then coffee_table_l1 19.5–22.5.
- Guitar: wardrobe_b1 0–17, bedroom_floor_b1 17–24 (the 03:00 sighting is wardrobe, not floor).

What would refute this fork: pan on the counter at 17:30; mug_omar in the cupboard at 18:00; guitar on the bedroom floor at 03:00.

